 "note": "Correct-answer key for the 460 catalogue questions, indexed by question id; the value is the 0-based position of the correct option in that question options array.",
 "why": "The official BAMF Gesamtfragenkatalog PDF does not mark correct answers. Every one of its 1800 checkboxes is the same empty-box glyph (U+F0A3, or U+25A1 in the questions added in the 2025 revision), and the file carries no solutions section. The key therefore cannot be derived from the catalogue and is kept here instead.",
 "verification": "Every one of the 460 answers was reviewed against the German question text. Three were wrong and have been corrected here: question 5 (free elections: the shipped key pointed at the prison option instead of freedom from coercion), question 71 (the Chancellor is most often in Berlin, not at Schloss Meseberg) and question 184 (Israel was founded on a UN resolution, not on a proposal by the German government). For 101 of the general questions the answer was independently confirmed against BAMF's own interactive Fragenkatalog at oet.bamf.de, which marks the correct option in its HTML. All 101 agreed. That tool could not confirm the rest: it serves a slightly older revision of the catalogue, shuffles both question and option order, and renders its question text as an image, so questions sharing an option set (all the Bundesland questions do) cannot be told apart. The 37 answers that depend on a picture - the federal and GDR coats of arms, the EU flag, the ballot paper, the occupation-zone map, and the 16 state coats of arms and 16 state outline maps - were each checked against the image in public/images.",
